Operation: getReservationsSummary
Summary: Get brief summary for Reservations
Description: This operation fetches brief summary for the reservations and also supports the Global Parameter  MAX ROWS FETCH COUNT . By default this parameter is configured to support an overall fetch of  5000  Records in total, with maximum number of records that can be fetched at a time being  200  (limit). However, this parameter can be updated to support an overall fetch value being a valid number between  1  and  10000  with maximum number of records that can be fetched at a time being same i.e.  200  (limit).  Requests with an  offset  and  limit  sum exceeding the  MAX ROWS FETCH COUNT  configured would fail the request.    OperationId: getReservationsSummary
Tags: Reservation
Parameters:
  - hotelId (path, string, required): Unique ID of the hotel where reservations is being searched.
  - advancedCheckedIn (query, boolean, optional): This filter indicates if the reservation(s) has performed an Advance Check-In or not. Data fetched is for 30 days ahead of business date.
  - limit (query, integer, optional): This filter indicates number of records the API has to fetch.
  - offset (query, integer, optional): This filter is for the index or initial index of the set(page) being requested. If the index goes out of the bounds of the total set count then no data will be returned.
  - preRegistered (query, boolean, optional): This filter indicates whether the reservation is Pre-Registered for Internet Check-In or not. Data fetched is for 30 days ahead of business date.
  - arrivalDate (query, string, optional): This filter is for the date of arrival of reservation.
  - departureDate (query, string, optional): This filter is for the date of departure of reservation.
  - createDateTime (query, string, optional): This filter is for the business date when reservation(s) was created in the system.
  - cancelledOn (query, string, optional): This filter is for the date when reservation(s) was cancelled.
  - folioClosedOn (query, string, optional): This filter is for the date when reservation(s) folio was closed.
  - lastName (query, string, optional): This filter looks up reservations with this last Name. Data fetched is for +-2 business date only when passed alone.
  - companyId (query, number, optional): This filter is ID of the company used for the reservation. Data fetched is for +-2 business date only when passed alone.
  - guestNameId (query, number, optional): This filter is ID of the guest.
  - reservationStatus (query, string, optional): This filter is computed reservation status of the reservation(s).
  - confirmationNumber (query, string, optional): This filter is ID of confirmation for the reservation.
  - externalReferenceNumber (query, string, optional): This filter is ID of external reference for the reservation.
  - cancellationNumber (query, string, optional): This filter is ID of cancellation for the reservation.
  - membershipNumber (query, string, optional): This filter is used for looking up reservations with this membership number. Last Name is required along with membership number to filter the data.
  - registeredCardNumber (query, string, optional): This filter is unique identifier of the registration card number. Last Name is required along with registration card number to filter the data.
  - balance (query, number, optional): This filter checks reservations with balance amount greater than or equal to this amount. Departure date is required along with balance to filter the data.
  - roomId (query, string, optional): This filter is for room number.
  - x-externalsystem (header, string, optional): External system code.
